    "type": "question",
    "label": "14",
    "prompt": "First introduce a pronumeral and then solve the equation.\n\n$\\$400$ is to be shared among three friends. David gets $\\$8$ more than Jennifer who gets $\\$16$ more than Brett. How much does each of the friends receive?",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "Brett: $\\$120$; Jennifer: $\\$136$; David: $\\$144$.",
      "worked": "Let Brett receive $x$ dollars. Jennifer receives $(x+16)$ dollars and David receives $(x+24)$ dollars.\n$$\\begin{align*}x+(x+16)+(x+24)&=400\\\\3x+40&=400\\\\3x&=360\\\\x&=120\\end{align*}$$\nBrett receives $\\$120$.\nJennifer receives $\\$(120+16)=\\$136$.\nDavid receives $\\$(120+24)=\\$144$.\n\nCheck: $120+136+144=400$, $136-120=16$ and $144-136=8$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 66
  },
